Z||000011||artherd||12-20-2001||06:51 AM||||add up 10-12 days worth of hours at the average local body shop rate...<P>Then multiply that by whatever number you like!  You've got a *croner* on the market here dude, this could be what you need to stuff an LT1 under there!<P>Don't sell yourself short, whatever you do.  It's insane, but people would rather pay $10k for a certin level of work than they would pay $100 for same.  Then they got 'Ten grand' worth of mods to their car.  It's called percived value.<P>I was once with a speaker manufactuer who had a retailer come to him and say "We love your speakers, but we can't sell them! Double your prices, please!!!"<P>He did, they sold oodles of them.<P>PS: I thought I distinctly heard you say you had spent over $2,000.00 in parts alone on your car, right?  I think you misplaced a zero on your orgional figure above, right? RIGHT!?!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: remenber, this guy is not only buying parts, 10-12 days of your LIFE, but he's also buying your knowledge and expertise on smoothing Fieros... which *no one else* has!<P>Keep the rarity (and largely thus, value) of both your car and your skill in mind before you do all four cars for a grand or something.<P>The Mona Lisa is valueable because there is only ONE...<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: I really dig your car, I can't wait to see it finished and painted!<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
